Lunacy's file picker.

webOS served a file picker as system UI at
/usr/lib/luna/system/luna-systemui/app/FilePicker/filepicker.html, and enyo.FilePicker (in
Enyo 1) opens exactly that path in an iframe, passing its parameters in the query string and
taking the result back through postMessage. Lunacy serves its own page there, so the control
works for every app without any app being changed.

Palm's picker listed what the media indexer had in db8. Lunacy has no media indexer, so this
one reads the same folders directly, through Lunacy's own service. The code is Lunacy's; the
contract it keeps (parameters, result shape, path) is webOS's, read from Enyo 1.0's
FilePicker.js and CrossAppUI.js, and its crop step follows Palm's ImagePicker and
ImageCropView (the reference TouchPad's systemui).

The "ringtone" type is Palm's own ringtone picker (source/RingtonePicker.js follows Palm's
FilePickerApp, RingtonePicker and AudioPicker, with its list fed by Lunacy's service rather
than db8). These are the TouchPad's files, copied unchanged from
/usr/lib/luna/system/luna-systemui/app/FilePicker on 2026-11-04:

- palm/AudioItem.js; palm/FPAudioPlayer.js (the FPAudioPlayer kind from AudioPicker.js);
- css/AudioPicker.css, css/RingtoneItem.css;
- images/: highlighticon.png, icn-play.png, icn-pause.png, icn-music.png, checkmark.png,
  empty-folder-audio.png, progress-item.png, progress-item-inner.png, multi-select-9tile.png,
  menu-icon-add-ringtone.png.

